  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Two different wires having lengths <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and respective temperature coefficient of linear expansion&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></math> are joined end-to-end. Then the effective temperature coefficient of linear expansion is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "KrulK",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "TmLie",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msqrt></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "dA9OE",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e1YIg",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The wire are joined end-to-end, so they are in series combination, then total&nbsp;length of wire is given by<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>When the temperature is increase by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></math>, then its final length is given by using concept of linear expansion,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Using equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> for the series combination of wires, final length is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math></p>",
